{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he saw Amalek.</b> And it is written: ״וירא את הקיני״ etc. These two nations he took together, because Amalek was the first of hatred and the Kenite the first of love, for through him officers of thousands and officers of hundreds were appointed. And for both of them he explains their recompense: Amalek — ״עדי אובד״; and the Kenite — ״איתן מושבך״, ״ושים בסלע קנך״, ״ושים שם דבר״ — that is: your dwelling and your nest shall be set on rock."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:09.610631942Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}